| `check_Y` ADR number spaces | Refuses an ADR file outside its number space, a malformed name, or a number used twice in one space. Bounds configured widths against both file-name byte limits before allocation; policy pattern faults give one key-naming FAILURE finding. | `make check` | [`adr.project_dir`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`adr.template_adrs`](settings.md#configprojectjson) | Judges names and numbers, not the decision. Review judges the decision. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
